.venv/
# The build interpreter's virtualenv (DECISIONS.md 15.8). Separate from .venv
# because it is python.org's universal2 framework build, not Homebrew's.
.venv-build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# The reading log is personal data, not source.
data/
server.log

# Front end (Phase 2). web/dist is committed as of Phase 4 -- FastAPI serves it.
web/node_modules/
web/*.tsbuildinfo

# Frozen bundle output (DECISIONS.md 15). Anchored with a leading slash so these
# never match the tracked web/dist.
/packaging/dist/
/packaging/build/

# build-send-workflow.md is deliberately NOT ignored, and the rule that ignored
# it (e9db79d, "gitignored it") is gone rather than negated -- it named that one
# file and protected nothing else. It is the procedure for `make send`, the one
# operation with a silent failure mode: a hand-rolled `ditto` zip skips the check
# at Makefile:32, and a fixed filename makes the recipient open last week's build
# with no symptom (DECISIONS.md 15.8.1). Untracked it existed on one disk and did
# not survive a clone. It holds no secrets.

# Release zips. Anchored to the repo root so nothing under web/ or packaging/ is
# caught by accident. A glob rather than a fixed name on purpose: `make zip`
# date-stamps the artifact (DECISIONS.md 15.8.1) and it belongs in
# packaging/dist/, so a rule naming one filename would stop covering it the
# moment the name changes -- which is exactly how a 15 MB build artifact came to
# be sitting at the repo root.
/*.zip

# Finder droppings. Not source, and not this project's business.
.DS_Store

# REVIEW.md is deliberately NOT ignored, and the rule that ignored it is gone
# rather than negated -- it was grouped in with .DS_Store, which is how a
# substantive document came to be treated as a Finder dropping. It is the record
# of the V1 review, both AUDIT.md and DECISIONS.md cite it by section, and
# AUDIT.md's blocker table is meaningless without it. Untracked it existed on one
# disk and would not have survived a clone. It holds no secrets.
